1. **No Significant Difference in Overall Mortality**: The most significant finding was that there was no significant difference in overall mortality rates between the two methods. After an average of 10 years, the overall mortality rates were 10.5% in the ACVBP + Cessification branch and 12.5% in the CHOP + RT branch.

