","The study of ancient fossils to study DNA, known as paleogenetics or paleogenenyology, is a challenging but groundbreaking field. The process involves several steps to extract and sequence genetic material from ancient organisms, which can then be used to study evolutionary relationships and potentially contribute to the possibility of future species-based research.

