","The concentration of hydonium ions \([H_3O^+]\) is given as \(10^{-4}\) M. The concentration of hydroxide ions \([OH^-]\) can be calculated using the ion product of water (\(K_w\)):  
\[
K_w = [H_3O^+][OH^-] = 10^{-14} \text{ at 25°C}
\]  
