The $n$-th vector is given by:
$$ a_n = a_1 + (n-1)(a_n - a_{n-1}) = (-2015, 14) + (n-1)(1, 1) = (-2015 + n - 1, 14 + n - 1) = (-2016 + n, 13 + n). $$

The magnitude of the $n$-th vector is:
$$ \left|a_n\right| = \sqrt{(-2016 + n)^2 + (13 + n)^2}. $$

To find the minimum value of $|a_n|$, we minimize the square of the magnitude:
$$ |a_n|^2 = (-2016 + n)^2 + (13 + n)^2. $$

Let $f(n) = (-2016 + n)^2 + (13 + n)^2$. To find the minimum value, we can take the derivative with respect to $n$ and set it to zero:
$$ f'(n) = 2(-2016 + n)(1) + 2(13 + n)(1) = -4032 + 2n + 26 + 2n = 4n - 4006. $$
Setting $f'(n) = 0$, we get:
$$ 4n - 4006 = 0 \implies n = \frac{4006}{4} = 1001.5. $$

