3. **Show \( f \) is bounded and continuous.**  
   - \( f \) is bounded because \( f(x) \leq 1 \) for all \( x \).  
   - \( f \) is continuous because \( C \) is closed, so \( f \) is continuous on \( C \) and \( f \) is continuous on \( C^c \) (the complement of \( C \)) because \( f \) is zero on \( C^c \).  

4. **Apply condition (i) to \( f \).**  
   - Since \( f \) is bounded and continuous, condition (i) implies:  
     \[
     \lim_n \int f \, d\mu_n = \int f \, d\mu.
     \]  
     This implies:  
     \[
     \lim_n \int f \, d\mu_n = \int 1 \, d\mu \text{ on } C \text{ and } \int 0 \, d\mu \text{ on } C^c.
     \]  
     Thus, \( \lim_n \int f \, d\mu_n = \int 1 \, d\mu \text{ on } C \text{ and } 0 \text{ on } C^c \).  

