   \[
   \gamma = \frac{(0.286 \times 10^{-9})^2}{2 \times 26 \times 10^9} = 1.02 \times 10^{-18} \text{ J/m}.
   \]

5. **Assume \(\rho_0\)**:
   The critical number density \(\rho_0\) is typically on the order of \(10^{18} \text{ dislocations/m}^3\).

6. **Substitute into the Oegger-Taylor equation**:
