","The typical range of outcomes for measurements of the Σ⁺ rest energy is determined by the uncertainty in the measurement. The lifetime of the particle is related to the width of the energy level in the energy spectrum due to the Heisenberg uncertainty principle. The uncertainty in the energy \(\Delta E\) is inversely proportional to the lifetime \(T_{1/2}\):

