6. Higgs boson decaying into a pair of tau leptons (ττ): This decay mode has a branching ratio of about 2%. This decay mode is sensitive to the Higgs boson's coupling to tau leptons.

7. Higgs boson decaying into a pair of muons (μμ): This decay mode has a branching ratio of about 0.2%.

8. Higgs boson decaying into a pair of electrons (ee): This decay mode has a branching ratio of about 0.01%.

The branching ratios of these decay modes can be used to infer various properties of the Higgs boson and the interactions it interacts with. For example, the branching ratios of the Higgs boson to W and Z bosons can be used to infer the mass of the Higgs boson and the coupling strength between the Higgs boson and these bosons. The branching ratios of the Higgs boson to quarks and leptons can be used to infer the mass of these particles and the coupling strength between the Higgs boson and these particles.

