\]

where \(\mathcal{D}\) is the matrix element of the \(S\)-matrix, \(\mathcal{S}\) is the matrix element of the \(S\)-matrix, and \(\Delta(E)\) is the phase factor. 

The unitarity condition is:

\[
\sum_l S_{lm}^* S_{ln} = \delta_{mn}.
\]

Using the definition of the \(S\)-matrix, we substitute \(S_{lm}\) and \(S_{nl}\):

\[
\sum_l \left( \frac{1}{e^{i\Delta(E)}} \mathcal{D}_{lm} \mathcal{S}_{lm} \right)^* \left( \frac{1}{e^{i\Delta(E)}} \mathcal{D}_{nl} \mathcal{S}_{nl} \right) = \delta_{mn}.
\]

